# KUDIX — BACKEND DEVELOPMENT SPECIFICATION

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Build a secure, scalable backend for KUDIX, an online gaming and rewards platform.

The backend must power user authentication, gaming credits, referral tracking, game access, six interactive games, social tasks, screenshot verification, referral commissions, gaming signals, notifications, customer support, and a comprehensive administrator dashboard.

The backend must connect to a separately developed frontend built with HTML, Tailwind CSS, and JavaScript.

The frontend and backend must communicate through secure APIs.

## 2. RECOMMENDED TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use the following technologies:

- Node.js for the server runtime.
- Express.js for REST API development.
- PostgreSQL for the primary database.
- Prisma ORM for database access and migrations.
- Secure authentication using established authentication libraries.
- Redis for caching, rate limiting, and temporary game-round coordination where necessary.
- WebSockets for real-time notifications and customer support messaging.
- Private object storage for uploaded task screenshots.
- A background job queue for notifications and other asynchronous operations.

Use environment variables for secrets and configuration.

Provide a complete setup guide, database schema, API documentation, migrations, and deployment instructions.

## 3. USER AUTHENTICATION

Implement a complete authentication system.

Required features:

- User registration.
- User login.
- Secure logout.
- Email or phone verification, according to the selected registration method.
- Password hashing.
- Password reset.
- Session management.
- Account status management.
- Protection against brute-force login attempts.
- Rate limiting on sensitive endpoints.

Each registered user must have a unique user ID and referral code.

Store user information securely.

Never store passwords as plain text.

Use secure, HttpOnly, appropriately configured cookies or another suitable token strategy.

## 4. WELCOME GAMING BONUS

When a new user successfully registers, automatically credit their account with ₦20,000 in promotional gaming credit.

The ₦20,000 welcome bonus is intended exclusively for playing eligible games on KUDIX.

It is not withdrawable and must never be treated as cash.

Requirements:

- Automatically issue the welcome bonus once per eligible account.
- Record the bonus in an immutable transaction ledger.
- Prevent duplicate bonus issuance.
- Maintain a separate promotional gaming credit balance.
- Prevent promotional gaming credits from being withdrawn.
- Allow eligible games to consume gaming credits according to their published rules.
- Record every credit allocation, deduction, reversal, and adjustment.
- Prevent negative balances and duplicate transactions.

The welcome bonus must be configurable through the admin dashboard.

All balance updates must be performed securely on the server, never trusted directly from frontend JavaScript.

## 5. REFERRAL SYSTEM

Implement a complete referral tracking system.

Each user must receive a unique referral code and referral link.

Requirements:

- Record the referring user during registration.
- Prevent users from referring themselves.
- Prevent duplicate referral relationships.
- Validate eligible registrations.
- Detect suspicious referral activity.
- Track referral status.
- Display referral progress in the user dashboard.
- Maintain a referral history.

Users must complete three eligible referrals before gaining access to games.

The required number of referrals must be configurable by an administrator.

Only verified, eligible referrals should count toward the requirement.

Implement appropriate safeguards against duplicate accounts, automated registrations, and referral abuse.

## 6. REFERRAL COMMISSIONS

The default referral commission is ₦1,000 per successful eligible referral.

Requirements:

- Automatically calculate qualifying referral commissions.
- Maintain a separate referral commission ledger.
- Record the referring user, referred user, amount, status, and timestamp.
- Prevent duplicate commission issuance.
- Allow administrators to review commission records.
- Support pending, approved, paid, reversed, and rejected statuses where appropriate.
- Provide a transaction history for each user.

Referral commissions must remain separate from promotional gaming credits.

Only eligible, approved commissions may become withdrawable, according to the published platform rules.

If withdrawals are introduced, implement a secure withdrawal workflow with appropriate authorization, verification, and audit logging.

Do not automatically convert the ₦20,000 promotional bonus into withdrawable cash.

## 7. GAME ACCESS CONTROL

Create a centralized game-access service.

A user must satisfy the platform's eligibility requirements before accessing protected games.

The default requirement is three successful eligible referrals.

Requirements:

- Verify the user's referral status on the server.
- Enforce access restrictions on every protected game API.
- Prevent users from bypassing restrictions by calling APIs directly.
- Return clear access-denied responses.
- Support configurable eligibility requirements.
- Record relevant access events.

The frontend must never be the sole authority for determining whether a user can access a game.

## 8. GAME ENGINE

Implement the following six games:

### A. Colour Prediction
Available outcomes:
- Red
- Green
- Black
- Yellow

### B. Number Prediction
Users select an available number.

### C. Heads or Tails
Available outcomes:
- Heads
- Tails

### D. Up or Down
Available outcomes:
- Up
- Down

### E. Lucky Number
Users select a number from the configured options.

### F. Higher or Lower
Users predict whether the next card's value will be higher or lower than the displayed card.

Each game must support configurable rules and a consistent server-side game engine.

### Game Engine Requirements

Implement:

- Game configuration.
- Game activation and deactivation.
- Round creation.
- Round scheduling.
- Round opening and closing.
- Prediction submission.
- Server-side validation.
- Round result publication.
- Game history.
- Result verification.
- Gaming credit deductions, where applicable.
- Appropriate error handling.
- Audit logging.

Use database transactions to ensure that prediction submissions and credit deductions remain consistent.

Prevent duplicate submissions, replay attacks, and concurrent requests from causing duplicate deductions.

Use secure server-generated identifiers for rounds and transactions.

## 9. GAME RESULTS AND ADMIN CONTROLS

The administrator needs a dashboard for managing games and their rounds.

The admin must be able to:

- Configure game options.
- Enable or disable games.
- Configure round durations.
- Create and schedule rounds.
- Open and close rounds.
- Publish official results.
- View submitted predictions.
- View round histories.
- Review game activity.

### Result Integrity

Implement a transparent and auditable result-management process.

If the administrator publishes a result manually, record:

- Administrator ID.
- Game ID.
- Round ID.
- Previous state.
- New state.
- Timestamp.
- Reason for the change.

For games represented as random games, use an appropriate server-side random outcome process and document the rules.

Do not permit administrators to secretly change a completed round's result after seeing users' predictions.

If manual outcomes are required for demonstrations or special promotional rounds, clearly label those rounds and disclose their rules to participants.

## 10. SIGNALS SYSTEM

Implement a dedicated signals service.

Authorized administrators can publish predictions for upcoming rounds.

Each signal should contain:

- Signal ID.
- Game type.
- Round ID, where applicable.
- Predicted outcome.
- Publication timestamp.
- Expiry time, where applicable.
- Publication status.
- Final result, once available.

Users should be able to retrieve current and historical signals through the API.

Support publishing announcements to an integrated channel when configured.

Signals must be distinguished from official results and must not be presented as guaranteed winning predictions.

Maintain a history of published signals and any permitted corrections.

## 11. SOCIAL TASKS SYSTEM

Implement a social task management service.

Administrators must be able to:

- Create tasks.
- Edit task descriptions.
- Set task instructions.
- Configure rewards.
- Activate or deactivate tasks.
- Set submission deadlines.
- Review submissions.
- Approve or reject submissions.
- Provide rejection reasons.

Users must be able to:

- View available tasks.
- Open task instructions.
- Submit screenshot evidence.
- View submission status.
- View administrator feedback.

### Screenshot Uploads

Use private object storage.

Requirements:

- Validate file types and file sizes.
- Generate safe server-side object names.
- Reject unsupported files.
- Prevent executable uploads.
- Keep uploaded evidence private.
- Authorize access to submitted screenshots.
- Use short-lived signed URLs when appropriate.

### Submission Statuses

Support:

- Pending.
- Under Review.
- Approved.
- Rejected.

If a task has a reward, credit it only after the appropriate approval and eligibility checks.

Prevent duplicate rewards for the same submission.

Record every review and reward transaction.

## 12. CUSTOMER SUPPORT CHATBOT

Implement a customer support service with chatbot functionality.

The chatbot should support common questions about:

- Registration.
- Welcome bonuses.
- Game access.
- Referrals.
- Referral commissions.
- Social tasks.
- Account settings.
- Gaming rules.

Users must also be able to request assistance from a human support agent.

Required features:

- Create support conversations.
- Send and receive messages.
- Maintain conversation history.
- Assign conversations to authorized agents.
- Track conversation status.
- Notify users when agents respond.
- Allow agents to close resolved conversations.

Use WebSockets or another appropriate real-time messaging method.

Enforce authorization so users can access only their own support conversations.

If an external chatbot or messaging provider is used, keep its API credentials on the server.

## 13. USER NOTIFICATIONS

Implement an in-app notification system.

Notify users about:

- Successful registration.
- Welcome bonus allocation.
- Referral progress.
- Referral commission status.
- Game access eligibility.
- Game results.
- New signals.
- Social task reviews.
- Support replies.
- Important platform announcements.

Store notifications in the database and allow users to mark them as read.

Support email, SMS, or other delivery methods only when configured.

## 14. ADMINISTRATOR AUTHENTICATION AND AUTHORIZATION

Implement a separate, secure administrator access system.

Requirements:

- Secure administrator login.
- Role-based access control.
- Strong password policies.
- Optional multifactor authentication.
- Session expiration.
- Login rate limiting.
- Administrative activity logs.
- Permission checks on every admin endpoint.

Suggested roles:

- Super Administrator.
- Game Manager.
- Task Reviewer.
- Support Agent.

Each role must have only the permissions required for its responsibilities.

Never rely on hidden frontend buttons or client-side checks to secure administrator functionality.

