## 17. API STRUCTURE

Organize the backend into versioned REST APIs.

Suggested endpoints:

### Authentication
- POST /api/v1/auth/register
- POST /api/v1/auth/login
- POST /api/v1/auth/logout
- POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password
- POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password

### User
- GET /api/v1/users/me
- GET /api/v1/users/dashboard

### Gaming Credits
- GET /api/v1/wallet
- GET /api/v1/wallet/transactions

### Referrals
- GET /api/v1/referrals
- GET /api/v1/referrals/stats
- GET /api/v1/referrals/link
- GET /api/v1/referrals/commissions

### Games
- GET /api/v1/games
- GET /api/v1/games/:gameId
- GET /api/v1/games/:gameId/rounds
- POST /api/v1/games/:gameId/predictions
- GET /api/v1/games/:gameId/history

### Signals
- GET /api/v1/signals
- GET /api/v1/signals/:signalId

### Social Tasks
- GET /api/v1/tasks
- POST /api/v1/tasks/:taskId/submissions
- GET /api/v1/tasks/submissions

### Notifications
- GET /api/v1/notifications
- PATCH /api/v1/notifications/:notificationId/read

### Support
- POST /api/v1/support/conversations
- GET /api/v1/support/conversations
- GET /api/v1/support/conversations/:conversationId/messages
- POST /api/v1/support/conversations/:conversationId/messages

### Administration
- GET /api/v1/admin/dashboard
- GET /api/v1/admin/users
- GET /api/v1/admin/games
- POST /api/v1/admin/games
- PATCH /api/v1/admin/games/:gameId
- POST /api/v1/admin/rounds
- POST /api/v1/admin/rounds/:roundId/results
- POST /api/v1/admin/signals
- POST /api/v1/admin/tasks
- GET /api/v1/admin/task-submissions
- PATCH /api/v1/admin/task-submissions/:submissionId
- GET /api/v1/admin/support/conversations

All endpoints must include suitable authentication, authorization, validation, and error handling.

## 18. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Implement:

- Input validation.
- Output encoding where appropriate.
- SQL injection prevention.
- Cross-site scripting protections.
- CSRF protection where applicable.
- Rate limiting.
- Secure CORS configuration.
- Secure cookie settings.
- Password hashing.
- File upload validation.
- Authorization checks.
- Audit logging.
- Database backups.
- Error monitoring.
- Protection against replay attacks.
- Idempotency for sensitive financial operations.

Never expose database credentials, authentication secrets, storage credentials, or private API keys to the frontend.

